course: dictionary
lesson: 15753
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Mum trimmed the hedge in the garden.» Here trimming means cutting a little off so the hedge looks tidy.
explain: The same word can name something different. «Lily sewed a gold trimming around the edge of her dress.» A trimming here is decoration, like lace or ribbon, not a cut. Ask yourself: is someone cutting something, or adding something pretty?
explain: At Christmas, «We had roast turkey with all the trimmings» means the turkey came with extra foods such as stuffing, potatoes and gravy. Trimmings is a noun, so it names things. When trimming means making something smaller, as in «trimming costs», it is a verb about reducing.
fact: Trim means to cut a little off something to make it tidy.
fact: «Trimming» can mean cutting, decoration, or making something smaller, so check the context.
fact: «The trimmings» are the extra foods served with a main dish, especially at Christmas in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Trimmings can also be the small bits that have been cut off.
fact: «Just a trim» means a small cut, such as a haircut that only takes off a little.
exercise: «The barber gave Sam just a trim.» What does trim mean here? | *A small cut to make hair tidy | A big Christmas dinner | A loud noise | A large, bright ribbon
exercise: «Mia sewed a pink lace trimming on her skirt.» What is the trimming? | A piece cut off the hedge | A small bird | *Decoration added to the edge | A type of food
exercise: «The council is trimming its budget this year.» What does trimming mean? | Adding a lot more money | Hiding it under a table | *Reducing it a little | Painting the walls
test: «Dad trimmed the grass at the edge of the lawn.» What does trimmed mean? | Painted it green | Watered it with a hose | *Cut a little off to make it tidy | Pulled up every plant
test: «Grandma's roast had all the trimmings: stuffing, sprouts and gravy.» What are the trimmings? | Plates for the guests | Turkey bones | Ribbons for the table | *Extra foods served with the main dish
exam: «The gold trimming on the coat shone in the sun.» What is the trimming? | Gold paint sprayed on the wall | *Decoration added to the edge of the coat | A type of hat | A cut-off piece of cloth
